(1980,'TOC - Standard Function - Wiki Help','Generate a table-of-contents for a page from the headings.','@@protect(true)
##Image(Wiki Help/TightWiki Logo.png | 15)
##title ##Tag(Official-Help | Help | Wiki | Official | Standard Function)
{{{Card(Default | Table of Contents) ##toc }}}

${metaColor = #ee2401}
${keywordColor = #318000}
${identifierColor = #c6680e}
==Overview
The TOC standard function is displays a table of contents based on the head tags in the page. Each heading will be linked to the header anchors to allow skipping directly to a given section. By default. the table of contents is built in the order that the page headings are found thereby creating a reasonable document outline. However, you can override this behavior by passing true to the alphabetized parameter. When alphabetized, the table retains the basic hierarchy, but the members are order alphabetically.


==Prototype
##Color(${keywordColor} | **#{ ##TOC }#**)(##Color(${keywordColor} | bool) {##Color(${identifierColor} | alphabetized)})


===Parameters
{{{Bullets
**Name:** ##Color(${identifierColor} | alphabetized) ##Color(${metaColor} | {Optional})
>**Type:** ##Color(${keywordColor} | bool)
>**Default:** ##Color(${identifierColor} | false)
>**Description:** Whether the table of contents is alphabetized or ordinal based.
}}}

==Examples
{{{Code(wiki)#{
##TOC

##TOC(true
}#}}}

==See Also
[[Function Calling Convention - Wiki Help]]
[[Scope Function - Wiki Help]]
[[Instruction Function - Wiki Help]]
[[Standard Function - Wiki Help]]


==Related
##related
