(2002,'Standard Function - Wiki Help','Standard functions are general use functions used by contributors to build a page and make it dynamic.','##title ##Tag(Draft)
{{{Card(Default | Table of Contents) ##toc }}}

==Overview
Standard functions are general use functions used by contributors to build a page and make it dynamic. These are functions that can be used to set the page tags, add a title, or drop in a glossary based on some search terms.


==Functions
##TagGlossary(Standard Function)


==Related
##related
',1,1,'12/5/2022 7:40:27 PM'),
(2003,'Alert - Scope Function - Wiki Help','Alerts bring important information to the attention of the reader.','@@protect(true)
##Image(Wiki Help/TightWiki Logo.png | 15)
##title ##Tag(Official-Help | Help | Wiki | Official | Scope Function)
{{{Card(Default | Table of Contents) ##toc }}}

${metaColor = #ee2401}
${keywordColor = #318000}
${identifierColor = #c6680e}
==Overview
The Alert scope function allows you to create a basic panel that contains wiki formatted text. Creating an alert is accomplished by three opening curly brackets which denote the scope of the alert, then alert function call with the parameters that define the type of alert within parenthesis. Next would be the content of the alert which is then terminated with three closing curly brackets.

Unlike [[Card - Scope Function - Wiki Help|cards]], a header is optional for alerts.



==Prototype
##Color(${keywordColor} | **#{ Alert }#**)(##Color(${keywordColor} | string) {##Color(${identifierColor} | styleName)} | ##Color(${keywordColor} | string) {##Color(${identifierColor} | titleText)})


===Parameters
{{{Bullets
**Name:** ##Color(${identifierColor} | styleName) ##Color(${metaColor} | {Optional})
>**Type:** ##Color(${keywordColor} | string)
>**Default:** ##Color(${identifierColor} | default)
>**Values:** ##Color(${identifierColor} | default, primary, secondary, light, dark, success, info, warning, danger)
>**Description:** The style of the alert.
**Name:** ##Color(${identifierColor} | titleText) ##Color(${metaColor} | {Optional})
>**Type:** ##Color(${keywordColor} | string)
>**Description:** The header of the alert, this is displayed at the top of the alert as a large header text.
}}}

==Examples
**Standard alert:**
{{{Code(wiki)#{
{{{ Alert(Primary)
This is the body content.
}}}
}#}}}

**Alert with a header:**
{{{Code(wiki)#{
{{{ Alert(Primary | This is the header)
This is the body content.
}}}
}#}}}


==See Also
[[Function Calling Convention - Wiki Help]]
[[Scope Function - Wiki Help]]
[[Instruction Function - Wiki Help]]
[[Standard Function - Wiki Help]]


==Related
##related
